    "id": "train-5326",
    "question": "Colin ran his first mile in 6 minutes.  He ran his next two miles in 5 minutes each and finished his 4th mile in 4 minutes.  What was the average time it took him to run a mile?",
    "gold": "5",
    "answer": "His first mile was in 6 minutes, then 5 minutes, another 5 minutes and his final mile was 4 minutes so it took him 6+5+5+4 = <<6+5+5+4=20>>20 minutes\nIt took 20 minutes to run 4 miles so his average time was 20/4 = <<20/4=5>>5 minutes per mile\n#### 5"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average time it took Colin to run a mile, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total time Colin took to run all four miles.\n2. Divide the total time by the number of miles to find the average time per mile.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total time Colin took to run the four miles. He ran his first mile in 6 minutes, his next two miles in 5 minutes each, and his fourth mile in 4 minutes. So, we add these times together:\n\n\\[\n6 + 5 + 5 + 4 = 20 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the average time per mile. We do this by dividing the total time by the number of miles:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{20 \\text{ minutes}}{4 \\text{ miles}} = 5 \\text{ minutes per mile}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the average time it took Colin to run a mile is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
